---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Pneumatic Actuators for Chemical Processing | Corrosion Protection | PNEUMACTUATOR"
  description="Corrosion-resistant pneumatic valve actuators for chemical plants: epoxy-coated rack and pinion and scotch yoke actuation, NAMUR accessory integration and ATEX options for classified areas."
>
  <section class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-night-green">INDUSTRIES · CHEMICAL PROCESSING</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Pneumatic Actuators for Chemical Processing</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-300">Corrosion-resistant quarter-turn actuation for aggressive media — epoxy-coated rack and pinion and scotch yoke packages with NAMUR accessory integration and ATEX options.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <!-- 应用背景 -->
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-blue">APPLICATION BACKGROUND</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Automating Valves That Handle Aggressive Media</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Chemical plants automate valves on reactors, dosing skids, transfer and storage lines that handle acids, solvents, caustics and slurries. Quarter-turn ball, butterfly and plug valves are common across this service, automated for on-off control, dosing and isolation. Batch and continuous processes alike depend on valves cycling on schedule, and pneumatic actuation suits the environment because it is simple, fast and tolerant of the washdown that keeps chemical plants clean.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Corrosion protection is the first question in chemical service. The actuator lives in the plant environment — vapors, spills, washdown chemicals — and housing coating, fastener material, shaft material and enclosure sealing decide how long it stays serviceable. Epoxy-coated housings with stainless steel fasteners are common choices, and in severe exposure, higher-grade materials and sealed enclosures are available. The right protection level depends on the actual exposure at each location, and confirming material options with the factory before ordering is the standard practice.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Control and mounting standards matter just as much. NAMUR (VDI/VDE 3845) standardizes the interface for solenoids, limit switches and positioners, so accessories mount directly on the actuator in a compact package with no loose brackets, while ISO 5211 governs the actuator-to-valve connection. Many chemical plants have classified hazardous areas, so the certification of the complete assembly — actuator plus accessories — should be checked against the plant's zone plan. Modulating flow control on dosing and transfer services adds a positioner with feedback on top of the same actuator family.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Beyond corrosion, chemical plants add two practical demands. The first is documentation: material certificates, test records and certification paperwork are routinely requested at project handover, and a factory that can issue them without friction saves weeks on the critical path. The second is standardization: plants that standardize on one actuator brand and a small set of accessory types cut the spare parts inventory and maintenance training, and they can keep a small stock of complete units for unplanned swaps. Where valves are automated for safety duties, the fail-safe position — spring return to close or open — is set by the plant's safety review, and the actuator is sized so the spring torque covers the valve at its worst expected condition.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 推荐产品表 -->
      <div class="mt-16">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-blue">RECOMMENDED ACTUATORS</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Actuator Families for Chemical Processing Duty</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-6 py-3.5 font-semibold">Actuator family</th>
                <th class="px-6 py-3.5 font-semibold">Typical duty</th>
                <th class="px-6 py-3.5 font-semibold">When it fits</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950"><a href="/products/rack-and-pinion/" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline">Rack and pinion</a></td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">On-off ball and butterfly valves</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Compact double acting actuation with NAMUR direct-mount accessories</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50/60">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950"><a href="/products/spring-return/" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline">Rack and pinion spring return</a></td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Fail-safe isolation valves</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Fail-close or fail-open when air supply is lost</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950"><a href="/products/rack-and-pinion/" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline">Rack and pinion + positioner</a></td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Dosing and flow control valves</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Modulating control with position feedback</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50/60">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950"><a href="/products/scotch-yoke/" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline">Scotch yoke</a></td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Large or high torque valves</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">High torque at stroke ends for big bore ball and plug valves</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">PNEUMACTUATOR covers 8 Nm to 200,000 Nm output torque. Corrosion protection grade, NAMUR accessories and ATEX certification are confirmed per plant site and zone.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 关键考虑点 -->
      <div class="mt-16">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-blue">KEY CONSIDERATIONS</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">What to Check for Chemical Processing Actuation</h2>
        <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Corrosion protection:</span> coating, fastener and shaft materials should match the actual exposure — vapors, spills and washdown chemicals around the actuator.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Hazardous area:</span> if the plant area is classified, the complete assembly — actuator plus solenoid, limit switch, positioner — needs certification for the zone, gas group and temperature class.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">NAMUR integration:</span> VDI/VDE 3845 pattern for direct-mount accessories; ISO 5211 for the valve interface.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Media and temperature:</span> aggressiveness and temperature of the media, and how the plant environment around the actuator changes with it.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Washdown:</span> sealed enclosures and IP rating for regular cleaning cycles.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Torque margin:</span> size against the valve torque curve at operating pressure, including seat friction effects.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Fail-safe:</span> spring return to the defined position for isolation and safety-related duties.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ -->
      <div class="mt-16">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-blue">FAQ</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Chemical Processing Actuation Questions</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950">What does NAMUR mean for pneumatic actuators?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">NAMUR refers to the VDI/VDE 3845 standard that defines the mounting pattern for accessories — solenoid valves, limit switches and positioners — on quarter-turn actuators. It lets accessories mount directly on the actuator in a compact, aligned package instead of on loose brackets, which simplifies installation and keeps the assembly tidy and predictable.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950">How is the actuator protected from corrosion in a chemical plant?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The usual package is an epoxy-coated housing with stainless steel fasteners and a sealed switch enclosure, and for heavier exposure, higher-grade materials and more aggressive coating options are available. The right level depends on what the actuator is exposed to — vapors, spills, washdown chemicals — so it is worth confirming material options with the factory for your specific area.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950">Do actuators in chemical plants need ATEX certification?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Only where the area is classified as hazardous. If the plant's zone plan places the valve in a classified zone, the complete assembly — actuator and its electrical accessories — must carry certification for that zone, gas group and temperature class. If the area is unclassified, standard industrial packages are the norm. Check the zone plan before specifying.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Need Corrosion-Resistant Actuators for Your Plant?"
    subtitle="Send your valve sizes, media, exposure conditions and zone classification — we confirm materials, NAMUR accessories and certification within 24 hours. Email sales@pneumactuator.com."
  />
</Layout>
